/edgar/data/1760965/000176096526000030/0001760965-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0001760965-26-000030"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-0.1% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760965/000176096526000030/0001760965-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0001760965-26-000030"}],"bear":[{"text":"Debt of $1.1bn against equity of $618.9m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760965/000176096526000030/0001760965-26-000030-index.htm","accession":"0001760965-26-000030"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.6% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760965/000089706926001538/0000897069-26-001538-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 46.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.46,"consecutive":2,"current":0.537,"current_display":"53.7%","threshold_display":"46.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 22.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.22,"consecutive":2,"current":0.45,"current_display":"45.0%","threshold_display":"22.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halv